{
  "id": "COMPOUND:36014 - PROTEIN:3691",
  "verbalization": "Jasplakinolide Z1 is implicated in the regulation of Arginine deiminase through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Jasplakinolide Z1 acts as a target for multiple entities, including Isoleucine--tRNA ligase and CEM-SS, which in turn are targets of (23r,24s)-3beta,11alpha,16beta,23,24-Pentahydroxy-5alpha-cholestan-6-one and (+)-Parviflorol, respectively. These compounds are all linked to Arginine deiminase, indicating a potential pathway where Jasplakinolide Z1 may influence the activity of Arginine deiminase through the modulation of these intermediaries. The final scores from the paths suggest a plausible but not definitive link, with the highest confidence in the direct interaction between Jasplakinolide Z1 and Arginine deiminase through the intermediaries mentioned. The mechanism likely involves the inhibition or regulation of enzymes involved in the arginine deiminase pathway, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action and the role of the intermediaries.",
